# Line endings: the repository stores LF and every checkout gets LF, whatever the local
# `core.autocrlf` setting. Prettier enforces `endOfLine: lf` for the sources it checks, so a
# CRLF checkout (the Git for Windows default) would otherwise fail `pnpm format:check`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Markdown uses two trailing spaces as a hard line break (see .editorconfig), so trailing
# whitespace is content there rather than a `git diff --check` error.
*.md whitespace=-blank-at-eol
